            <ArticleTitle>Ultrasound and CT imaging assessment of renal angiomyolipoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr.01.2010.2624</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr0120102624</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report a case of a 41-year-old woman who was admitted to the emergency department of our hospital because of acute right flank pain. Laboratory investigations and cultures were negative. A transabdominal ultrasonography revealed a large mass of the upper pole of the right kidney as an incidental finding.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
